==English==

===Etymology===
Latinate variant of [[Lucy]], or today borrowed from modern Italian. Name of a Sicilian martyr, {{etyl|la}} Lucia, feminine form of the Roman [[praenomen]] [[Lucius]], from {{term|lux|lang=la}} "light".

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{given name|female|from=Latin}}.

